                            "output": "{\n  \"状态\": \"成功\",\n  \"结果\": [\n    \"{<file_title>Chen和Hou-2003：A mixed multiscale finite element method for elliptic problems with oscillating coefficients.pdf</file_title>\\n<file_abstract>【文档类型】：论文  \\n【摘要】：本文提出了一种混合多尺度有限元方法，用于解决具有快速振荡系数的二阶椭圆方程。通过使用过采样技术，该方法能够在不解析所有细尺度结构的情况下捕捉解的宏观结构。数值实验表明，该方法在模拟具有随机对数正态相对渗透率的多孔介质流动传输时具有高效性和准确性。</file_abstract>\\n<paragraph_content>Throughout we are interested in the fractional fow curves. A fractional fow curve $F(t)$ attime $t$ is defined as the production rate on $\\\\Gamma_{\\\\mathrm{out}}$ by the following formula: \\n$$\\nF(t)=\\\\Big(\\\\int_{0}^{1}\\\\ v_{1}(1,x_{2},t)(1-S(1,x_{2},t))\\\\ d x_{2}\\\\Big)\\\\Big/\\\\Big(\\\\int_{0}^{1}\\\\ v_{1}(1,x_{2},t)\\\\ d x_{2}\\\\Big).\\n$$\\nHere $1\\\\mathrm{~-~}S$ stands for the saturation of the produced fuid (e.g., oil), and thus $F(t)$ represents the percentage of the produced oil over water. We also use the dimensionless time PVI in our computations. One PVI is the time required to fill the whole reservoir by injecting water at $\\\\Gamma_{\\\\mathrm{in}}$ . It is equal to [12] \\n$$\\nP V I=\\\\frac{t v_{1}^{\\\\mathrm{average}}L_{2}}{L_{1}L_{2}}=t v_{1}^{\\\\mathrm{average}},\\n$$</paragraph_content>}\",\n    \"{<file_title>Chen和Hou-2003：A mixed multiscale finite element method for elliptic problems with oscillating coefficients.pdf</file_title>\\n<file_abstract>【文档类型】：论文  \\n【摘要】：本文提出了一种混合多尺度有限元方法，用于解决具有快速振荡系数的二阶椭圆方程。通过使用过采样技术，该方法能够在不解析所有细尺度结构的情况下捕捉解的宏观结构。数值实验表明，该方法在模拟具有随机对数正态相对渗透率的多孔介质流动传输时具有高效性和准确性。</file_abstract>\\n<paragraph_content>AMIXEDMULTISCALE FINITE ELEMENT METHOD \\nBy Cauchy's inequality and (4.25) we obtain \\n$|\\\\,\\\\mathrm{III}_{1}|\\\\leq C\\\\|\\\\,\\\\nabla u_{\\\\varepsilon}-\\\\nabla u_{1}^{\\\\varepsilon}\\\\,\\\\|_{0,K}\\\\|\\\\,\\\\nabla W_{0}^{S}\\\\,\\\\|_{0,K}\\\\leq C\\\\|\\\\,\\\\nabla u_{\\\\varepsilon}-\\\\nabla u_{1}^{\\\\varepsilon}\\\\,\\\\|_{0,K}\\\\|\\\\,\\\\mathbf{q}_{h}\\\\,\\\\|_{0,K}.$ Next, by the argument used in deriving (4.24) and by Lemma 4.9, we have \\n$\\\\begin{array}{r}{|\\\\operatorname{III}_{2}|\\\\leq C(\\\\varepsilon+h_{K})\\\\|\\\\,u_{0}\\\\,\\\\|_{2,K}\\\\|\\\\,\\\\mathbf{q}_{h}\\\\,\\\\|_{\\\\mathrm{div},K}+C\\\\varepsilon h_{K}^{\\\\frac{d}{2}-1}\\\\|\\\\,u_{0}\\\\,\\\\|_{1,\\\\infty,K}\\\\|\\\\,\\\\mathbf{q}_{h}\\\\,\\\\|_{\\\\mathrm{div},K}.}\\\\end{array}$ Since $\\\\partial G_{i}^{j}(x,y)/\\\\partial y_{i}=0$ in $Y$ , integration by parts gives \\n$$\\n\\\\int_{Y}G_{i}^{j}(x,y){\\\\frac{\\\\partial\\\\chi^{k}}{\\\\partial y_{i}}}(x,y)\\\\,d y=0.\\n$$\\nThus, again by the argument used in deriving (4.24) and by Lemma 4.9, we get \\n$$</paragraph_content>}\"\n  ]\n}",
